===Etymology===
From {{inh|ba|trk-pro|*bal|t=honey}}.

Cognate with
{{cog|cjs|пал|t=honey}},
{{cog|tr|bal|t=honey}},
{{cog|cv|пыл|t=honey}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ba|[bɑɫ]}}
* {{audio|ba|Ba-бал.oga|audio:}}
* {{hyphenation|ba|бал}} ''(one syllable)''

===Noun===
{{ba-noun}}

# [[honey]]
#: {{ux|ba|Сәскә '''балы'''.|translation=Flower '''honey'''.}}
#: {{ux|ba|Йүкә '''балы''' тәмле, хуш еҫле, ҙур дауалау көсөнә эйә.|translation=Linden '''honey''' is palatable, has a pleasant smell ''(and)'' great medicinal properties.}}
#: {{ux|ba|Башҡорт '''балына''' һорау йылдан-йыл арта бара.|translation=The demand '''for''' Bashkir '''honey''' has been growing year after year.}}
# [[mead]]; alcoholic drink fermented from honey and water

